  "label": "intended audience",
  "description": "The meme is designed to target and provoke individuals who hold racist, anti-Black ideologies, particularly those who support or are sympathetic to systemic disenfranchisement of Black Americans. The hateful text 'what if i told you blacks should not vote' is explicitly directed at Black people, using the visual of a peaceful civil rights protest to amplify its message. The target audience is likely those who are either unaware of or deliberately ignore the historical and ongoing struggle for Black voting rights, and who may be susceptible to racist rhetoric that denies Black people's civic legitimacy. The meme functions as a tool to spread hate speech by invoking historical and systemic racism, making its primary target community those who are predisposed to or receptive to anti-Black stereotypes and exclusionary political messaging.",
